e chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=-3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =-2, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot (3) \\\\  & =(6)+(-9) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529475 1080 "-4" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529475 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529475 1083 #uuid "45b5b453-6b35-5cc4-af2b-e39ebc8096ef" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529476 1080 "2" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529476 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529476 1083 #uuid "47a9714a-7491-5ba7-88a6-5362405ded8c" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529477 1068 #edb/ref 17592186529472 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529477 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529477 1071 "Let $f(x,y)=3 x + y,$ where $x=- 2 s - 3 t$ and $y=s - 3 t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529477 1072 #uuid "4a433498-d0db-5e2d-80cc-422f4772f109" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529477 1074 "![](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(3)\\cdot (-3)+(1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =(-9)+(-3) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529478 1080 "-4" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529478 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529478 1083 #uuid "4a5aca8d-e4a3-529a-930a-8ba48fc7c160" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529479 1080 "8" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529479 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529479 1083 #uuid "4dc0a3e7-a98e-5719-b23a-809d76a9431d" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529480 1068 #edb/ref 17592186529470 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529480 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529480 1071 "Let $f(x,y)=2 x - 3 y,$ where $x=s - t$ and $y=2 s - 2 t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" 13194139535820 17592186045443 true] [17592186529480 1072 #uuid "592d650a-7aa0-5957-9d77-7248908a6bf